  "worked_solution": "Since $-4{x}^{2}-1$ is always negative, we can divide both sides of the inequality by this quantity, but we have to remember to flip the sign of the inequality. By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-4{x}^{2}-1)(3x-2) & <0 \\\\ \\frac{(-4{x}^{2}-1)(3x-2)}{-4{x}^{2}-1} & >\\frac{0}{-4{x}^{2}-1} \\\\ 3x-2 & >0 \\\\ x & >\\,\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
